    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "To document a use case for this feature: the [HogWild! algorithm](http://papers.nips.cc/paper/4390-hogwild-a-lock-free-approach-to-parallelizing-stochastic-gradient-descent) requires atomic floating-point addition. While that may be achievable in Numba's CUDA support, we need atomic intrinsics (ideally applicable to NumPy arrays, an intrinsic atomic `arr[i] += x` operation) in order to make such implementations that work without a GPU.",
    "created_at": "2019-10-08T19:55:46Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/2988#issuecomment-539676146",
