  {
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Yes. I don't love the API, but it does work: https://github.com/KatanaGraph/katana/blob/master/python/katana/numba_support/numpy_atomic.py (The project is BSD licensed)\r\n\r\nIdeally there would be some way to mark a normal array access as needing atomic code gen. \r\n\r\nMy hack directly generates LLVM instructions for the atomics. It should also implement CAS loops for operations that are not available as single LLVM instructions, but it doesn't yet.\r\n\r\n*My code may be memory management unsafe:* The system it's used with only uses very limited compiled functions and they are always called synchronously from within a python call, so we don't need to reference count anything.\r\n\r\nI hope this code is useful.",
    "created_at": "2021-04-12T18:27:45Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/2988#issuecomment-818031151",
    "id": 818031151,
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/numba/numba/issues/2988",
    "node_id": "MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgxODAzMTE1MQ==",
    "performed_via_github_app": null,
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "+1": 1,
      "-1": 0,
      "confused": 0,
