  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "CC @arthurp, @Sfonxu \n\nFor the record, the `numpy_atomic.py` file referenced above has moved to:\nhttps://github.com/KatanaGraph/katana/blob/master/python/katana/native_interfacing/numpy_atomic.py\n\nI confirm it used to work great ([used in the PySDM project](https://github.com/open-atmos/PySDM/blob/main/PySDM/backends/impl_numba/atomic_operations.py)), however this workaround does not seem to work on ARM CPUs. Any ideas on how to achieve atomic operations in multi-threaded Numba JIT-compiled code on ARM CPUs warmly welcome!",
